WEBVTT

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.330
Biwa.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.660
The color of your eye changed.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.670
Perhaps Biwa has inherited Father's eye.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.750
Freaky!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.750
Maybe you're a specter.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.880
I mean, you never get any bigger.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.970
What?!

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.130
Why, you little...

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.300
Sukemori!

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.720
See, she's a <i>bakeneko</i>!

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.430
--Stop it, Biwa!
--Biwa, enough!

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.100
Brother!

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.480
What a lively bunch.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.310
Lord Munemori.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:46.860
I though surely you
would be in low spirits.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:52.070
Or is this just how you behave with
your strict father no longer around?

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.280
Munemori.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.120
I have come today to
inform my late brother,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.040
that I shall take firm hold of the reigns.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.170
As head of the Heike!

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:18.220
THE HEIKE STORY

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:37.380
Episode 5

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.100
Oh, you're so cute!

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.690
Good job!

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.440
There, there!

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.900
Tokuko.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.200
Tomomori, dear brother.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.280
My, His Highness is standing splendidly!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.040
And here we have...
one of Shigemori's attendants...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.040
Biwa.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.380
Your eye is the same as his!

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.300
Did Brother have a love child?

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.420
You are mistaken.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.510
Oh, sorry!

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:20.050
I just assumed. You know, even
the emperor has his other child...

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.600
Forgive me!

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.230
I've stuck my foot in
my mouth twice in a row!

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.860
My son has a little brother now.
Through a different mother.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.200
Kogo?

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.740
No, someone else. Lady Shokuko.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.750
So your wife has become
that child's wet nurse?

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.380
Uh, yeah... she has.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.630
And you have become
Munemori's adjunct, right?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.220
Yeah. Alongside our
little brother Shigehira.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.470
Is Munemori actually ready
to be clan head, I wonder?

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.180
Hmm, well, uh...

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.930
How is Father?

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:13.400
I hear that he's been holed up in
Fukuhara since Shigemori passed.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.030
The shock must have hit him hard.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.530
Anyway,

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.740
we can't feel down forever.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.580
Even without Shigemori, we must
carry the Taira clan forward.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.420
We'll combine our brotherly strength
and work heartily and nimbly!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.340
What a vexing bug.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.550
Now then,

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.140
you say that damned Kiyomori
is still out of it?

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.220
Yes.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.350
Then he's just a senile old man now.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.150
What a great opportunity.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.370
It was Emperor Go-Shirakawa?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.460
Yes.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:16.710
He seized the province of Echizen
that Koremori inherited...

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:24.970
...and the Fujiwara assets that Moriko had
taken possession of were also seized...

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.770
And lately...

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:33.900
...he has also been meddling
with regard to court positions.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.440
Curses!

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.480
Father?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.780
How dare he? Curse him!

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.410
Father?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.860
F-Father!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.120
F-F-F-F-Father!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.830
Munemori, gather troops!

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.290
I'm returning to the capital.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.880
I'm not senile yet!

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.640
You! Make way! Make way!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.800
It's Lord Kiyomori.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.930
He intends to retaliate.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.900
Father, welcome back to the capital.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:25.780
Munemori!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:26.620
Yes!

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.320
Tomomori!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:27.910
Sir!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:28.820
Shigehira!

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.240
Yes.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.700
Beginning today,

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:37.130
we dismiss the regent, the chancellor,
and 41 others from their offices.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:41.250
Afterwards, the positions
will be filled from the Heike.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.760
And as for Motofusa, who took
away Shigemori's territory,

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.180
exile him to Hyuga!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.930
Move out! Go! Go!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.770
--Open the gate!
--Circle there too!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.020
Capture them all!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.400
Don't resist!

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.480
I beg your pardon!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:07.610
Spare me exile to Hyuga! For I have
taken vows and renounced the world!

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.700
In that case, I shall let you
off with exile in Bizen.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.530
Munemori!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.120
Yes, Father!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.000
Go to Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.250
We will have His Majesty
reside at the Toba Palace.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.750
You mean to confine His Majesty?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.260
To go so far seems--

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.590
I shall go at once, Father!

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.560
Even me?

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:39.350
What gall. For the Heike warriors
to bare their fangs at me...

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.280
It's outrageous!

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:46.700
I'll never forgive this, Kiyomori!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:11.760
The Yata Mirror, the Ama-no-Murakumo
Sword, and the Yasakani Magatama.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.600
The Three Sacred Treasures are
proof that you are the emperor!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.600
The youngest in history
to accede to the throne!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.360
I'd say "infantile" rather than "young."

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.360
Tokuko, you should rejoice.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.490
Your child--my grandson--
has become the emperor!

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.490
Haven't you?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.660
His Majesty understands
this is a happy thing.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.250
Now then...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.080
Retired Emperor Takakura!

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:50.090
I would love for you to visit
my Itsukushima Shrine!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.520
Uncle Shigehira, you play so well!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.610
High praise from you, Kiyotsune.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:09.860
Should you really be standing
around playing the flute?

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:17.200
Brother! Uncle is visiting out of concern
for us after the loss of Father!

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.870
Yes, but I also wanted to
get away from Munemori.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.380
It's still so cold.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.380
Hm, this one.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.970
The other day, he demanded Lord
Nakatsuna of the Genji's prized horse,

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.800
despite repeated refusal.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.890
So this is the famous horse
you treasure so much.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.770
I shall give this horse
the name Nakatsuna.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.150
Run, blasted Nakatsuna!

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.400
Blasted Nakatsuna,
feel the sting of my crop!

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.330
Tomomori and I
remonstrated with him later.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.250
Such behavior from
the head of the Heike...

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.290
And if Father were alive,

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.960
Emperor Go-Shirakawa would
never have been confined either.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:11.260
Given Emperor Takakura's visit to
Itsukushima Shrine despite opposition,

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.680
I expect the confinement will end soon.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:19.430
I imagine Emperor Takakura went along with
Father's request with that goal in mind.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.730
Father is too high handed.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:25.100
Anyway, your concern is
understandable, Sukemori.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.900
But going forward,
<i>we </i>will be leading the Heike.

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:33.490
In preparation, we must take an interest
in governance as well as the flute,

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.320
and develop our fighting skills.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.160
Yes, Uncle!

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.870
You're not a <i>bakeneko</i>, but a puppy.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.990
"<i>Bakeneko</i>?"

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.700
Yeah, her.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.250
What with her eyes and all,
she's suspicious.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:49.500
Sukemori, if you don't fix the way you
speak, the court ladies will dislike you.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.420
As will the girl you fancy.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.760
I hear you were quite a help
to my brother Shigemori.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:01.390
If you ever have a problem, come to me.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.770
I shall assist you any time.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.570
That's how he treated your prized horse?

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:19.160
And they even branded it
with the name Nakatsuna!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:28.880
To think of my son Nakatsuna's pain
fills me with frustration and misery!

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:33.670
The late Lord Shigemori was a
considerate man of the utmost courtesy.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:37.970
But now, a great many dislike the Heike,
and even despise them!

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:42.720
Prince Mochihito, Your Highness is Emperor
Go-Shirakawa's second prince.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.640
You are exceptionally learned
and of fine lineage.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.400
There was even talk that you
would accede to the throne.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:53.070
True, that did not happen and your
talent has long gone unrecognized.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:56.440
But now, your abilities are needed!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.820
Bring down the Heike,
depose Emperor Antoku,

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.120
and become emperor yourself,
Your Highness!

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:06.160
I beg you, harden your resolve!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.580
Give us your command!

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:22.720
Prince Mochihito ordered
the downfall of the Heike?!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:27.640
I hear the command is presently
circulating to the Genji in all quarters.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.640
Inform my father in Fukuhara at once!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.650
Yes, sir!

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:34.650
Seize the prince immediately
and exile him to Tosa!

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.480
I'm returning to the capital!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.910
Speak! Where is Prince Mochihito?

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.360
Search the entire estate!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.870
Capture them all!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:49.250
I never expected word
would get out this early.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.040
It is all right. The coast is clear.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.550
Your Highness, hide at Onjoji Temple
until the Genji forces have gathered.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.260
Father! We awaited your arrival!

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.360
I am told Prince Mochihito narrowly
escaped to Onjoji Temple dressed

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.400
as a woman.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:20.150
But if the Heike attack...

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.410
Onjoji's strength will not suffice,

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:28.660
so they sought help from Enryakuji on
Mt. Hiei and Kofukuji in Nara. But...

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.410
This rice is ours!

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.580
You already took plenty!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.540
I sent 20,000 <i>koku </i>of Omi Province
rice to Enryakuji.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.460
Wow, Father. What a brilliant move!

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.800
Now Enryakuji will side with the Heike.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.800
But what about Kofukuji?

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:48.560
We don't need both.
A bird cannot fly with one wing plucked.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:53.230
Prince Mochihito apparently
left Onjoji to head for Kofukuji.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:56.440
He must intend for them to harbor him.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:02.700
A report arrived! Prince Mochihito
has entered Byodoin Temple.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.860
Byodoin, you say?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:07.950
Word is he was exhausted on the road
and fell six times from his horse.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.330
He is currently resting at Byodoin.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.330
This is our opportunity! Attack Byodoin!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.840
Tomomori, you go as a general.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:17.330
Yes, Father!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.340
You, too, Shigehira.

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:19.840
Yes, sir.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.130
And lastly...

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.640
Well, Mother, I must depart now.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.100
Koremori.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.430
Brother, may you have fortune in battle.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.730
Brother, you can't defeat the enemy
if you're poised to run like usual.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.080
I can't sleep with the
racket you're making.

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.500
I'm surprised you could
hear it over the rain.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:06.090
Brother has been a
scaredy-cat since childhood.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:11.220
He's more suited to dancing
than swinging a sword.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.850
Do you think he'll be all right?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.650
♬ 28,000 riders for the Heike ♬

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:23.860
♬ crossed the Kowata Mountains
and advanced on Uji Bridge. ♬

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.500
♬ Behold! ♬

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:40.090
♬ Attack! Attack! ♬

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:43.960
♬ However... ♬

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.510
They've removed the bridge! Be careful!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.260
♬ ...the rear troops did not hear this ♬

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:54.060
♬ and in their race forward ♬

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:59.350
♬ 200 riders were pushed over
the edge and swept away. ♬

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:03.820
♬ Then, both sides stood at opposite
ends and exchanged volleys. ♬

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:11.200
♬ Into the fray advanced
Tajima of Gochiin Temple, ♬

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.870
♬ wearing no armor, holding no shield. ♬

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:17.210
♬ The arrows flying toward him
he sliced from the air! ♬

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.290
♬ Sliced them from the air! ♬

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.710
♬ Thus did he become known
as Tajima the arrow slicer. ♬

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.230
K-Keep it together!

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:43.980
Brother, we can't make use
of our numbers on this bridge.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.280
We should retreat.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.360
Retreat?!

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.450
Yes. Rather than do bridge battle,

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.570
let's cross the river and fight.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.570
How?

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.040
Ah, I see!

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.870
So this is how we can
withstand the current.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.470
No need for heroics.

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:14.600
Just stay calm and defeat who you can.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.940
Save any who fall in! Leave no one behind!

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:13.280
Yorimasa and Nakatsuna of Minamoto, who
urged Prince Mochihito to raise an army,

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.410
were cornered and killed
themselves at Byodoin!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:20.200
Prince Mochihito was hit with
an arrow as he fled and perished!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.210
To top it off, Onjoji Temple...

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:28.170
...why, Shigehira, you set it ablaze!

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:34.050
The battle lasted into nightfall.
The risk of friendly fire forced me to.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:36.010
The blaze just spread so quickly!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:39.560
Why, I find myself having
to praise my younger brother!

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:49.440
We had no other choice, right?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:51.480
Fighting is the warrior's way.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:54.240
When you fight, losing is not an option.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:02.370
After all this,
the Genji will think twice.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.170
There should be no more
battles for quite some time.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:18.970
So cute!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:19.970
Tokuko?

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.730
You seem down.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:32.230
Emperor Takakura spends
little time with my son lately.

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:36.150
I am told he had another
child with Lady Shokuko...

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:39.030
To think about it pains
and distresses me so...

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.620
I thought you didn't want this marriage.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.410
No, not at first.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.540
I wonder when that changed.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.710
Once, servants used the fallen leaves
of his beloved maple trees

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:54.010
as kindling to warm their saké.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:56.550
Everyone was aghast.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:59.720
"Warming my saké on
fallen leaves in the forest."

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:01.470
How elegant.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:05.180
That was his response.
He didn't rebuke them.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:07.390
He is a kind man.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.850
But...

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:13.110
Emperor Takakura must find it more
comforting to be with someone else

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.780
than with me.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:19.240
A daughter of Kiyomori, of the Heike...

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:25.660
Though they had different mothers,
Prince Mochihito was his older brother.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.630
Father... the Heike killed him.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.210
It's all so awful.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.500
But I choose to forgive.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:38.840
Father, Emperor Takakura,
Emperor Go-Shirakawa--all of them.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.050
Maybe that sounds presumptuous.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:44.970
But... someone has to forgive,

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.890
or there will be only hatred and conflict.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:52.610
But I'd like to think the world
isn't all pain and suffering.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:56.150
So I'll forgive, and forgive,

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.240
and forgive.

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:04.910
Pa?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.700
Did you forgive, Pa?

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.710
Shigemori,

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.750
did you forgive?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.920
Did <i>you </i>forgive, Biwa?
